  "rendered": "The separated cathode powder was calcined in air at 600 °C[1] for 2 h[2]. The stated purpose was to remove the surface coatings and the conductive carbon (CB) left on the recovered cathode material: to remove sur-[3] face coatings and CB.[4] The choice of temperature is supported by the TGA-DTG data: the organic coating layer loses about ~3.3 wt%[5] near ~350 °C[6], and CB loses about ~4.1 wt%[7] near ~550 °C[8], so both can be removed by calcining in air at 600[9] °C. ",
